e data lives**: Should it be one global todo list per user (in `~/.local/share/todo/` or `%APPDATA%`)? The alternatives are a per-directory list (like a `.todo` file in each project), or both, where a local file overrides the global one.\n\n➡️ One global list per user. Per-project lists can be added later if you find you need them.\n\n---\n\n❓ **Q6** - **Sync or multiple machines**: Does the list need to work across several machines (through Dropbox, a git-synced folder or a server), or does it only need to live on this one?\n\n➡️ This machine only. We'll keep the storage as a plain file so you can drop it in a synced folder later without any code changes.\n\n---\n\nAnswer each by number. \"Yes\" accepts my recommendation; otherwise just tell me what you want instead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":22149,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":573},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5e45304-d9ec-4d58-9f82-7f230f17ec9b","uuid":"815d1758-c834-49e9-8190-5c6fbf9ac134","timestamp":"2026-11-14T11:40:29.470Z","request_id":"req_011Ch2ksfUFhUCuCiBZJm1ew"}
